   "html_text": "Constructivism’s critics might adopt a similar skeptical attitude to the positive social role of political principles. Thus, they could grant that social unity, civic friendship and political autonomy are all desirable consequences that arise when some relevant agents affirm and conform to certain shared principles. The critics might also accept that if those principles really did resemble artifacts in the way constructivism assumes then such desirable functional properties would play some role ",
